<h1>A Little Bit of Gore</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Sound design &amp; foley <span class="ph">&middot; [2024] &middot; [team or studio name]</span></p>

<h2>Project overview</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <p>A Little Bit of Gore is a fast, cartoonishly violent [arena action] game in which every enemy bursts into confetti-coloured giblets. It's gory, but mostly it's funny.</p>
  <p>The brief was "disgusting, but in a way that makes you laugh", so the sound leans on exaggerated, rubbery foley rather than anything realistic.</p>
</div>

<h2>My role</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <ul>
    <li>Sound designer: impacts, gore, weapons and UI</li>
    <li>Foley recording and editing</li>
    <li>Creature vocals, performed and processed by me</li>
    <li>Implementation in [FMOD Studio and Unity] and the final mix</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2>Technical approach</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <p>Most of the gore came from one afternoon of foley: celery and carrots for bones, a wet chamois and cabbage for squelches, and a lot of tinned spaghetti.</p>
  <p>Each impact is built from three randomised layers (a body, a crunch and a wet tail), and a <i>combo</i> parameter adds extra layers and pitches everything up as the chaos escalates.</p>
</div>

